Name the caller that passes a NULL colour space, and the one that made the colour.

cocotron 0139 guards three O2ColorSpace entry points and prints __builtin_return_address(0) on the
NULL path. Nobody had read one, for a good reason: a bare return address needs the load map of a
process that has already exited. dladdr answers the image and the nearest exported symbol from
inside the run, so one drive names it.

DRIVEN, iA Writer to the Editor preferences pane, the path 0139 was written for. Forty NULL colour
spaces reach the guards, from exactly two places:

    CIDER_CSNULL model      image=AppKit  sym=+[NSColor colorWithCGColor:]+30      20 times
    CIDER_CSNULL components image=Onyx2D  sym=O2ColorCreate+263                    20 times

Both are downstream of one colour, so O2ColorCreate now says who built it when the space is NULL,
and that is the whole answer:

    CIDER_CSNULL create     image=InterfaceFoundation sym=IFColorSampleColor+35    20 times

InterfaceFoundation is a framework iA Writer ships inside its own bundle. Its IFColorSampleColor
passes NULL as the colour space, and the guards are what keep that survivable rather than a segfault
in a switch on a dereferenced NULL.

AND THE SILENCE ELSEWHERE IS NOW BOUNDED. The same switch over the other six roster applications on
the launch and resize path prints nothing, and that means something here because the instrument was
shown able to speak first: CIDER_TRACE_VIEWS uses the same fprintf to stderr from the same
framework, and 28 of its lines reach app.log in a run where CIDER_CSNULL prints none.
--- a/Onyx2D/O2ColorSpace.m
+++ b/Onyx2D/O2ColorSpace.m
@@ -20,6 +20,8 @@
